IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poca-nouns`

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, sections 333 to 333E (tipping off in the regulated sector) -- LAYER 1.   Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
-- Section 333 is blank in this text.  Section 333A makes it an offence for a person who works in the regulated sector to tell anyone that a disclosure has been made, or that an
-- investigation is being contemplated or carried out, when that is likely to prejudice the investigation.  Sections 333B to 333D list the disclosures that are permitted.
-- Section 333E says how the words are read.
--
-- SHAPE.  Each permitted disclosure is a BOOLEAN exception; each offence composes the exceptions: an exception that applies is JUST FALSE ("does not commit an offence under section 333A",
-- a flat negative, ruling N2); a failed element is JUST FALSE (lawyer-reading (a)); an element that is NOTHING (the Schedule 9 answer cannot say) makes the offence NOTHING.
-- The prohibition is derived from each offence as a SHANT with no WITHIN: the text states no period (ruling N2).
-- "Situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements" is an input, fed by s 333E(4).

§ `Sections 333 to 333E: tipping off`

-- s 333 is shown as a row of dots only: blank in this text (coverage table: repealed or blank in this text).

§§ `s 333A: the offences`

DECLARE `Recipient of the earlier disclosure (section 333A(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a constable`
    `an officer of Revenue and Customs`
    `a nominated officer`
    `a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of that Agency`
    `someone else`

-- src:257 | (2) The matters are that the person or another person has made a disclosure under this Part—
-- src:258 | (a) to a constable,
-- src:259 | (b) to an officer of Revenue and Customs,
-- src:260 | (c) to a nominated officer, or
-- src:261 | (d) to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of that Agency,
-- src:262 | of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 333A(2) (src:257-262)
GIVEN `the person or another person has made a disclosure under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `Recipient of the earlier disclosure (section 333A(2))`
      `the disclosure was of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(2) the matter is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person or another person has made a disclosure under this Part`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters are that the person or another person has made a disclosure under this Part" (a closed definition read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF recipient EQUALS `someone else` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters are ... (a) to a constable, (b) to an officer of Revenue and Customs, (c) to a nominated officer, or (d) to a National Crime Agency officer authorised" (a closed list read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF `the disclosure was of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector" (marginal reading (a))

-- src:253 | (1) A person commits an offence if—
-- src:254 | (a) the person discloses any matter within subsection (2);
-- src:255 | (b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in that subsection; and
-- src:256 | (c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 333A(1) (src:253-256)
GIVEN `the person discloses a matter within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business the information came to the person in` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the permitted disclosures of sections 333B to 333D applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception of section 333D(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(1) the person commits an offence by disclosing a matter within subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the permitted disclosures of sections 333B to 333D applies` OR `the exception of section 333D(3) applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under section 333A" (s 333B(1), (2), (4), s 333C(2), s 333D(1), (1A), (2), (3))
        IF `the person discloses a matter within subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if (a) the person discloses any matter within subsection (2)" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in that subsection`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted" (marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of that business`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business the information came to the person in` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the business is not "a business in the regulated sector" by Schedule 9 (s 333E(1))
        IF `the person discloses a matter within subsection (2)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business the information came to the person in` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether the matter is within subsection (2), or the business is in the regulated sector, is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:263 | (3) A person commits an offence if—
-- src:264 | (a) the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out;
-- src:265 | (b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation; and
-- src:266 | (c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 333A(3) (src:263-266)
GIVEN `the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business the information came to the person in` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the permitted disclosures of sections 333B to 333D applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception of section 333D(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333A(3) the person commits an offence by disclosing an investigation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the permitted disclosures of sections 333B to 333D applies` OR `the exception of section 333D(4) applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under section 333A" (s 333B(1), (2), (4), s 333C(2), s 333D(1), (1A), (2), (4))
        IF NOT (`the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if (a) the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation" (marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of that business`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector" (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2 for the business the information came to the person in` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as Schedule 9 says (NOTHING-kind, limited by its own wording, when Schedule 9 cannot say)

-- src:267 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:268 | (a) on summary conviction to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, or to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale, or to both;
-- src:269 | (b) on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or to a fine, or to both.
@ref s 333A(4) (src:267-269)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of being convicted`
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
`s 333A(4) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 333A` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 3, `ceiling of the fine` IS `level 5 on the standard scale`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 24, `ceiling of the fine` IS `a fine with no ceiling stated`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE

-- src:270 | (5) This section is subject to—
-- src:271 | (a) section 333B (disclosures within an undertaking or group etc),
-- src:272 | (b) section 333C (other permitted disclosures between institutions etc), and
-- src:273 | (c) section 333D (other permitted disclosures etc).
@ref s 333A(5) (src:270-273)
GIVEN `section 333B (disclosures within an undertaking or group etc) permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 333C (other permitted disclosures between institutions etc) permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 333D (other permitted disclosures etc) permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333A(5) one of the permitted disclosures of sections 333B to 333D applies` MEANS
    `section 333B (disclosures within an undertaking or group etc) permits it` OR `section 333C (other permitted disclosures between institutions etc) permits it` OR `section 333D (other permitted disclosures etc) permits it`

@ref s 333A(1) (src:253-256)
GIVEN `the answer under section 333A(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 333A(1) the person must not disclose a matter within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 333A(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `disclose a matter within section 333A(2)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 333A(1): the person disclosed a matter within subsection (2)"

@ref s 333A(3) (src:263-266)
GIVEN `the answer under section 333A(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 333A(3) the person must not disclose that an investigation is contemplated or is being carried out` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 333A(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `disclose the contemplated or actual investigation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 333A(3): the person disclosed that an investigation is contemplated or is being carried out"

§§ `s 333B: disclosures within an undertaking or group etc`

-- src:275 | (1) An employee, officer or partner of an undertaking does not commit an offence under section 333A if the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking.
@ref s 333B(1) (src:275)
GIVEN `he is an employee, officer or partner of an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333B(1) the disclosure within an undertaking is permitted` MEANS
    `he is an employee, officer or partner of an undertaking` AND `the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking`

-- src:276 | (2) A person does not commit an offence under section 333A in respect of a disclosure by a credit institution or a financial institution if—
-- src:277 | (a) the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution,
-- src:278 | (b) the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements, and
-- src:279 | (c) both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group.
@ref s 333B(2) (src:276-279)
GIVEN `the disclosure is by a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333B(2) the disclosure within a group of institutions is permitted` MEANS
        `the disclosure is by a credit institution or a financial institution`
    AND `the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution`
    AND `the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`
    AND `both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group`

-- src:280 | (3) In subsection (2) “group” has the same meaning as in Directive 2002/87/ EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16 th December 2002 on the supplementary supervision of credit institutions, insurance undertakings and investment firms in a financial conglomerate.
@ref s 333B(3) (src:280)
GIVEN `it has the meaning given in Directive 2002/87/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16th December 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333B(3) the institutions belong to the same group` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has the meaning given in Directive 2002/87/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16th December 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "group" has "the same meaning as in Directive 2002/87/EC", which is not among the sources

-- src:281 | (4) A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 333A if—
-- src:282 | (a) the disclosure is to professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser,
-- src:283 | (b) both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements, and
-- src:284 | (c) those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control.
@ref s 333B(4) (src:281-284)
GIVEN `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333B(4) the disclosure between advisers in undertakings under common control is permitted` MEANS
        `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
    AND `the disclosure is to a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
    AND `both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`
    AND `those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control`

§§ `s 333C: other permitted disclosures between institutions etc`

DECLARE `Kind of disclosure (section 333C(1))` IS ONE OF
    `by a credit institution to another credit institution`
    `by a financial institution to another financial institution`
    `by a professional legal adviser to another professional legal adviser`
    `by a relevant professional adviser of a particular kind to another relevant professional adviser of the same kind`
    `another disclosure`

-- src:286 | (1) This section applies to a disclosure—
-- src:287 | (a) by a credit institution to another credit institution,
-- src:288 | (b) by a financial institution to another financial institution,
-- src:289 | (c) by a professional legal adviser to another professional legal adviser, or
-- src:290 | (d) by a relevant professional adviser of a particular kind to another relevant professional adviser of the same kind.
@ref s 333C(1) (src:286-290)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of disclosure (section 333C(1))`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333C(1) this section applies to the disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `another disclosure` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a disclosure (a) by a credit institution to another credit institution, (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (a closed list read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:291 | (2) A person does not commit an offence under section 333A in respect of a disclosure to which this section applies if—
-- src:292 | (a) the disclosure relates to—
-- src:293 | (i) a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made,
-- src:294 | (ii) a transaction involving them both, or
-- src:295 | (iii) the provision of a service involving them both;
-- src:296 | (b) the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act;
-- src:297 | (c) the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements; and
-- src:298 | (d) the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data (within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3(2) and (14) of that Act)).
@ref s 333C(2) (src:291-298)
GIVEN `section 333C applies to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure relates to a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure relates to a transaction involving them both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure relates to the provision of a service involving them both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333C(2) the disclosure between institutions or advisers is permitted` MEANS
        `section 333C applies to the disclosure`
    AND (    `the disclosure relates to a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made`
          OR `the disclosure relates to a transaction involving them both`
          OR `the disclosure relates to the provision of a service involving them both`)
    AND `the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act`
    AND `the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`
    AND `the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data`

§§ `s 333D: other permitted disclosures etc`

-- src:300 | (1) A person does not commit an offence under section 333A if the disclosure is—
-- src:301 | (a) to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017; ...
-- src:302 | (aa) for the purposes of proceedings under section 336A (power of court to extend moratorium period);
-- src:303 | (ab) made in good faith by virtue of section 339ZB (disclosures within the regulated sector); or
-- src:304 | (b) for the purpose of—
-- src:305 | (i) the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere),
-- src:306 | (ii) an investigation under this Act, or
-- src:307 | (iii) the enforcement of any order of a court under this Act.
@ref s 333D(1) (src:300-307)
GIVEN `the disclosure is to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purposes of proceedings under section 336A (power of court to extend moratorium period)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in good faith by virtue of section 339ZB (disclosures within the regulated sector)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of an investigation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of the enforcement of any order of a court under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333D(1) the disclosure for one of the listed purposes is permitted` MEANS
        `the disclosure is to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017`
     OR `the disclosure is for the purposes of proceedings under section 336A (power of court to extend moratorium period)`
     OR `the disclosure is made in good faith by virtue of section 339ZB (disclosures within the regulated sector)`
     OR `the disclosure is for the purpose of the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)`
     OR `the disclosure is for the purpose of an investigation under this Act`
     OR `the disclosure is for the purpose of the enforcement of any order of a court under this Act`

-- src:308 | (1A) Where an application is made to extend a moratorium period under section 336A, a person does not commit an offence under section 333A if—
-- src:309 | (a) the disclosure is made to a customer or client of the person,
-- src:310 | (b) the customer or client appears to the person making the disclosure to have an interest in the relevant property, and
-- src:311 | (c) the disclosure contains only such information as is necessary for the purposes of notifying the customer or client that the application under section 336A has been made.
-- src:312 | “Moratorium period” and “relevant property” have the meanings given in section 336D.
@ref s 333D(1A) (src:308-312)
GIVEN `an application is made to extend a moratorium period under section 336A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a customer or client of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer or client appears to the person making the disclosure to have an interest in the relevant property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure contains only such information as is necessary for the purposes of notifying the customer or client that the application under section 336A has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333D(1A) the disclosure to a customer or client about the application is permitted` MEANS
        `an application is made to extend a moratorium period under section 336A`
    AND `the disclosure is made to a customer or client of the person`
    AND `the customer or client appears to the person making the disclosure to have an interest in the relevant property`
    AND `the disclosure contains only such information as is necessary for the purposes of notifying the customer or client that the application under section 336A has been made`

-- src:313 | (2) A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 333A if the disclosure—
-- src:314 | (a) is to the adviser’s client, and
-- src:315 | (b) is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence.
@ref s 333D(2) (src:313-315)
GIVEN `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to the adviser's client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333D(2) the disclosure by an adviser to dissuade the client is permitted` MEANS
    `he is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` AND `the disclosure is to the adviser's client` AND `it is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence`

-- src:316 | (3) A person does not commit an offence under section 333A(1) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(1)(b).
@ref s 333D(3) (src:316)
GIVEN `the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333D(3) the exception of section 333D(3) applies` MEANS
    `the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(1)(b)`

-- src:317 | (4) A person does not commit an offence under section 333A(3) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(3)(b).
@ref s 333D(4) (src:317)
GIVEN `the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 333D(4) the exception of section 333D(4) applies` MEANS
    `the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 333A(3)(b)`

§§ `s 333E: how the words are read`

-- src:319 | (1) For the purposes of sections 333A to 333D, Schedule 9 has effect for determining—
-- src:320 | (a) what is a business in the regulated sector, and
-- src:321 | (b) what is a supervisory authority.
@ref s 333E(1) (src:319-321)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(1) the business is a business in the regulated sector` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraphs 1 and 2` -- Schedule 9 decides; JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged

@ref s 333E(1) (src:319-321)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(1) the body is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 4` -- Schedule 9 decides; JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING pass through unchanged

-- src:323 | “credit institution” has the same meaning as in Schedule 9;
@ref s 333E(2) (src:323)
GIVEN `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(2) the institution is a credit institution` MEANS
    `the answer under Schedule 9 paragraph 1(2)` -- "has the same meaning as in Schedule 9"; the Schedule 9 answer passes through unchanged

-- src:324 | “financial institution” means an undertaking that carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of that Schedule.
@ref s 333E(2) (src:324)
GIVEN `it is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(2) the undertaking is a financial institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an undertaking` AND `it carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 9` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial institution” means an undertaking that carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of that Schedule"

-- src:325 | (3) References in those sections to a disclosure by or to a credit institution or a financial institution include disclosure by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf.
@ref s 333E(3) (src:325)
GIVEN `the disclosure is by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(3) the disclosure counts as a disclosure by or to the institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References ... to a disclosure by or to a credit institution or a financial institution include disclosure by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf"

-- src:326 | (4) For the purposes of those sections a country or territory imposes "equivalent money laundering requirements" if it imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU of the Council of 20th May 2015 on the prevention of the use of the financial system for the purpose of money laundering and terrorist financing, as amended by Directive 2018/843 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30th May 2018.
@ref s 333E(4) (src:326)
GIVEN `it imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU of the Council of 20th May 2015 on the prevention of the use of the financial system for the purpose of money laundering and terrorist financing, as amended by Directive 2018/843` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(4) the country or territory imposes equivalent money laundering requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU of the Council of 20th May 2015 on the prevention of the use of the financial system for the purpose of money laundering and terrorist financing, as amended by Directive 2018/843` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "equivalent" is measured against Directive 2015/849/EU as amended, which is not among the sources, so a failure cannot be shown from the text

-- src:327 | (5) In those sections “relevant professional adviser” means an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers (as the case may be) and which makes provision for—
-- src:328 | (a) testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission; and
-- src:329 | (b) imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards.
@ref s 333E(5) (src:327-329)
GIVEN a IS A `Adviser`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333E(5) the person is a relevant professional adviser` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a's `accountant, auditor or tax adviser` AND a's `member of a professional body established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers` AND a's `the body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership as a condition for such admission` AND (a's `the body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members` AND a's `the body makes provision for imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant professional adviser” means an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers and which makes provision for (a) ... and (b) ..." (a definition read as closed)
